[38;5;252m[1m## Key translation decision[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Byte-identical output required calling straight through to the host libc [38;5;10mstdio[0m ([38;5;10mprintf[0m, [38;5;10mfprintf[0m, [38;5;10mfopen[0m, [38;5;10mfgets[0m, [38;5;10mferror[0m, [38;5;10mfclose[0m, and the [38;5;10mstderr[0m global) rather than rebuilding on Rust's [38;5;10mstd::io[0m. The C code writes to both [38;5;10mstdout[0m and [38;5;10mstderr[0m, and the interleaving of those writes depends on libc's buffering mode — line-buffered on a TTY, block-buffered on a pipe, with [38;5;10mstderr[0m unbuffered. Rust's own buffers would flush at different points and reorder the output. [38;5;10msrc/cstdio.rs[0m holds those bindings; [38;5;10msrc/goto.rs[0m is the translated logic.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Each [38;5;10mgoto[0m collapsed into structured control flow: the forward jump in [38;5;10mforward_goto_example[0m became an early return; the shared [38;5;10mcleanup[0m label in [38;5;10mopen_with_cleanup[0m became a fall-through out of an [38;5;10mif[0m block, which preserves the fact that [38;5;10mfp[0m is null on one path and non-null on the other.[0m[0m
